1
00:00:37,120 --> 00:00:38,663
[Episode 1]

2
00:01:35,220 --> 00:01:37,623
Hey, everyone! The teacher's coming!

3
00:01:45,485 --> 00:01:47,223
Attendance!

4
00:01:47,223 --> 00:01:48,534
Kim Gi Ju.

5
00:01:49,317 --> 00:01:50,344
Kim Gi Ju?

6
00:01:50,344 --> 00:01:51,570
Yes, sir.

7
00:01:51,570 --> 00:01:52,960
Answer me on cue, okay?

8
00:01:52,960 --> 00:01:54,897
- Kim Ba Wool!
- Here!

9
00:01:54,897 --> 00:01:56,568
- Kim Seong Jin.
- Here.

10
00:01:56,568 --> 00:01:58,702
- Kim So Hee.
- Here.

11
00:01:58,702 --> 00:02:00,638
- Kim Ha Yeon A.
- Here!

12
00:02:00,638 --> 00:02:03,522
- Kim Ha Yeon B.
- Here.

13
00:02:03,522 --> 00:02:05,502
- Noh Jin Yeong.
- Here!

14
00:02:05,502 --> 00:02:07,068
- Park Jae Min.
- Here.

15
00:02:07,068 --> 00:02:08,590
- Park Hyeon Ah.
- Here.

16
00:02:08,590 --> 00:02:09,838
- Park Hye Yeong.
- Here.

17
00:02:09,838 --> 00:02:11,009
Seo Gyeong Jin.

18
00:02:11,009 --> 00:02:12,398
- Yang Yeong Min.
- Yup.

19
00:02:12,398 --> 00:02:14,073
- Lee Se Jun.
- Here.

20
00:02:14,073 --> 00:02:15,716
- Lee Ye Jae.
- Here.

21
00:02:15,716 --> 00:02:17,754
- Lee Yun Ah.
- Here.

22
00:02:17,754 --> 00:02:19,473
- Im Jae Gyeong.
- Here.

23
00:02:19,473 --> 00:02:20,803
Jang Ho Jae.

24
00:02:40,065 --> 00:02:42,726
Did you see it, Ha Yeon?

25
00:02:42,726 --> 00:02:44,956
- I saw this thing on YouTube yesterday--
- Yun Ah!

26
00:02:44,956 --> 00:02:46,280
Let's go to the restroom together.

27
00:02:46,280 --> 00:02:47,695
Okay!

28
00:02:56,476 --> 00:02:57,896
Kim Ha Yeon!

29
00:02:58,839 --> 00:03:00,166
No, not you.

30
00:03:00,166 --> 00:03:01,697
Me?

31
00:03:01,697 --> 00:03:03,074
You're B?

32
00:03:03,074 --> 00:03:05,600
What? No, I'm A.

33
00:03:05,600 --> 00:03:07,286
The teacher wants you, B.

34
00:03:08,111 --> 00:03:10,089
What are you doing, slacking off?

35
00:03:10,950 --> 00:03:12,150
Dancing.

36
00:03:12,150 --> 00:03:14,027
But you suck at dancing.

37
00:03:18,568 --> 00:03:20,660
Kim Ha Yeon B.

38
00:03:20,660 --> 00:03:22,748
What's your goal here?

39
00:03:25,163 --> 00:03:28,672
A mid-tier 4-year university in Seoul.

40
00:03:31,908 --> 00:03:33,275
And your ideal major?

41
00:03:35,298 --> 00:03:37,885
Whichever will have me, I guess.

42
00:03:39,682 --> 00:03:42,043
No specific dreams?

43
00:03:42,043 --> 00:03:43,937
Like, what do you want to be when you grow up?

44
00:03:44,738 --> 00:03:46,685
University...

45
00:03:46,685 --> 00:03:51,022
student... seems like a good place to start.

46
00:03:51,022 --> 00:03:52,290
That so?

47
00:03:52,290 --> 00:03:55,569
Well, then, let's see.

48
00:03:55,569 --> 00:03:57,237
We will...

49
00:04:02,117 --> 00:04:05,245
have to set our goal right around here.

50
00:04:08,890 --> 00:04:10,476
Okay. You can go.

51
00:04:21,909 --> 00:04:23,569
Alright, Teach...

52
00:04:34,563 --> 00:04:37,956
Yun Jae asked me if I wanted to
go on a trip with him yesterday.

53
00:04:37,956 --> 00:04:39,416
Do you think it'll be alright?

54
00:04:40,642 --> 00:04:41,725
For real?

55
00:04:41,725 --> 00:04:43,214
- Through the night?
- Yeah!

56
00:04:43,214 --> 00:04:44,230
The whole day.

57
00:04:44,230 --> 00:04:46,797
No way, what will you tell your parents?

58
00:04:46,797 --> 00:04:49,770
I'll just tell them I'm staying up
studying at a study cafe.

59
00:04:51,554 --> 00:04:52,771
What are you looking at?

60
00:04:54,878 --> 00:04:57,839
I saw the way you looked at me just now.

61
00:04:57,839 --> 00:05:00,330
This is pissing me off.

62
00:05:00,330 --> 00:05:01,495
Kim Ha Yeon.

63
00:05:01,495 --> 00:05:03,639
Get your head out of the gutter!

64
00:05:04,338 --> 00:05:06,223
- What? Me? No, I...
- Hey.

65
00:05:06,223 --> 00:05:08,518
You're the one with dirty thoughts, Heo Mi Hee.

66
00:05:08,518 --> 00:05:10,632
No, I'm not!

67
00:05:10,632 --> 00:05:13,345
Hey, hear this. Yesterday, Yun Jae and I...

68
00:05:15,167 --> 00:05:17,283
What do I do?

69
00:05:17,283 --> 00:05:21,380
- Well, I guess that calls for a condom.
- Hey!

70
00:05:21,380 --> 00:05:23,088
Come with me, you!

71
00:05:23,088 --> 00:05:25,894
What? You can say it here, come on!

72
00:06:05,532 --> 00:06:09,112
Hey, Kim Ha Yeon was being
such a cow today, don't you think?

73
00:06:10,161 --> 00:06:11,787
Wrong chat.

74
00:06:30,025 --> 00:06:33,845
[Reserved for firetrucks only]

75
00:06:49,258 --> 00:06:53,176
[Award]

76
00:06:55,728 --> 00:06:57,791
I'm home.

77
00:07:02,589 --> 00:07:06,461
Mom, I need money for my math workbook.
Just leave me 20,000 won.

78
00:07:06,461 --> 00:07:08,375
Use your textbook.

79
00:07:16,881 --> 00:07:19,155
There's no secret about my birth.

80
00:07:21,360 --> 00:07:23,452
Nor any special talents.

81
00:07:25,384 --> 00:07:26,853
No best friend.

82
00:07:26,853 --> 00:07:28,707
No boyfriend.

83
00:07:35,898 --> 00:07:37,067
Ha Yeon...

84
00:07:37,067 --> 00:07:39,031
Did you see that message?

85
00:07:39,031 --> 00:07:43,269
It's just that Yun Ah
kept saying bad things about you.

86
00:07:43,269 --> 00:07:45,127
It's fine, no big deal.

87
00:07:46,352 --> 00:07:47,714
I'm not kindhearted,

88
00:07:47,714 --> 00:07:50,717
but I can't bring myself to
stand up for myself, either.

89
00:07:51,359 --> 00:07:56,825
Then, Ha Yeon, can I borrow
the white sundress you bought last time?

90
00:07:56,825 --> 00:07:59,747
I was thinking of wearing it to see Yun Jae.

91
00:07:59,747 --> 00:08:00,793
Please?

92
00:08:09,331 --> 00:08:10,432
Sure.

93
00:08:17,591 --> 00:08:20,500
That little wench.

94
00:08:24,233 --> 00:08:28,384
I'm just a frayed curtain on a windowsill.

95
00:08:28,384 --> 00:08:31,412
A seldom-used dustpan and an old clock.

96
00:08:32,789 --> 00:08:36,064
An unused kettle at the back of the classroom,
or an abandoned cup,

97
00:08:36,064 --> 00:08:37,985
that's who I was...

98
00:09:59,098 --> 00:10:01,231
until I met you.

99
00:10:01,921 --> 00:10:05,772
[1. Kim Ha Yeon B]

100
00:10:05,772 --> 00:10:07,978
[Summer Vacation]

101
00:10:07,978 --> 00:10:09,019
Listen up.

102
00:10:09,019 --> 00:10:10,844
Don't waste all your time frolicking around.

103
00:10:10,844 --> 00:10:12,295
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, Teach!

104
00:10:12,295 --> 00:10:14,572
Less than half of senior year is left.

105
00:10:14,572 --> 00:10:16,192
- Yeah!
- Yes, sir!

106
00:10:16,192 --> 00:10:20,427
I said, more than half
of your senior year has passed!

107
00:10:20,427 --> 00:10:22,953
Go, now, go. You can leave.

108
00:10:22,953 --> 00:10:24,918
- Thank you, Teach!
- Thank you!

109
00:10:37,478 --> 00:10:40,842
The start of summer vacation means
the start of summer school.

110
00:10:40,842 --> 00:10:42,424
See you tomorrow. Roger, out.

111
00:10:42,424 --> 00:10:44,825
- No, no!
- Why is this happening?

112
00:10:44,825 --> 00:10:46,271
- Say no to summer school!
- Boo!

113
00:10:46,271 --> 00:10:48,507
This sucks major butt!

114
00:10:56,811 --> 00:10:59,535
Anyone want to go watch a movie
after class tomorrow?

115
00:11:00,553 --> 00:11:02,217
Oh, me, me!

116
00:11:02,217 --> 00:11:03,847
Me too, me too!

117
00:11:03,847 --> 00:11:05,595
What are we watching?

118
00:11:07,247 --> 00:11:08,896
Something raunchy.

119
00:11:08,896 --> 00:11:10,233
Something hot!

120
00:11:13,020 --> 00:11:14,484
Sounds fun.

121
00:11:14,484 --> 00:11:16,411
We'll watch it all together!

122
00:11:20,508 --> 00:11:22,611
I'm home.

123
00:11:23,933 --> 00:11:24,976
What are you doing, Mom?

124
00:11:24,976 --> 00:11:26,928
Kim Ha Yeon. Go start packing now.

125
00:11:26,928 --> 00:11:28,633
We'll get stuck in traffic
unless we leave right now.

126
00:11:28,633 --> 00:11:29,947
Where are we going?

127
00:11:29,947 --> 00:11:31,424
Jung Yeon!

128
00:11:35,883 --> 00:11:38,852
But Mom, can't I leave a week later?

129
00:11:38,852 --> 00:11:40,078
Why?

130
00:11:40,078 --> 00:11:41,489
Is it because of school?

131
00:11:41,489 --> 00:11:43,170
What, a group project or something?

132
00:11:43,170 --> 00:11:44,645
No, not that.

133
00:11:44,645 --> 00:11:47,503
I have a sign language lesson on Saturday.

134
00:11:47,503 --> 00:11:49,744
- Mom.
- How about this? We go now,

135
00:11:49,744 --> 00:11:51,819
and you can come back home
in time for your lesson.

136
00:11:51,819 --> 00:11:53,959
But for now, let's all leave together, okay?

137
00:11:53,959 --> 00:11:55,855
Come on, Mom's begging you.

138
00:11:55,855 --> 00:11:57,947
Please, Jung Yeon, please!

139
00:11:57,947 --> 00:11:59,397
Mom.

140
00:12:00,138 --> 00:12:02,941
- Darling!
- What the actual hell.

141
00:12:02,941 --> 00:12:06,303
Are these all the golf clubs?
Do we have everything?

142
00:12:06,303 --> 00:12:08,339
- Mom.
- I can't believe this.

143
00:12:08,339 --> 00:12:11,601
Where did the duffel bag go?

144
00:12:13,222 --> 00:12:14,780
Mom!

145
00:12:14,780 --> 00:12:16,144
What!

146
00:12:23,931 --> 00:12:28,757
Your dad's going to be the caddie
for pro golfer Cho Ji Hyeon this summer.

147
00:12:31,005 --> 00:12:33,511
We'll be spending the whole summer
at the Upo Country Club.

148
00:12:33,511 --> 00:12:34,932
No whining.

149
00:12:38,167 --> 00:12:40,147
What about my summer school?

150
00:12:40,147 --> 00:12:43,270
I-I need to attend those classes, you know.

151
00:12:43,270 --> 00:12:46,664
Are you sure you'll get
accepted to a university?

152
00:12:46,664 --> 00:12:47,701
What?

153
00:12:48,372 --> 00:12:51,769
I don't expect you to make it into a
SKY university, like your brother,

154
00:12:51,769 --> 00:12:53,883
but would any 4-year university in Seoul...

155
00:12:54,542 --> 00:12:56,251
accept you? At all?

156
00:12:56,251 --> 00:12:57,464
Mom.

157
00:12:57,464 --> 00:13:00,286
I'm doing my best, too, you know.

158
00:13:00,286 --> 00:13:02,655
Seriously.

159
00:13:02,655 --> 00:13:07,525
Working as a teacher all these years,
I've seen plenty of kids like you.

160
00:13:07,525 --> 00:13:12,753
They try their best, sure,
but nothing ever happens with them.

161
00:13:16,132 --> 00:13:20,052
- What?
- Kids like that are just pitiful.

162
00:13:20,052 --> 00:13:24,441
They're just wasting their time,
and will never amount to anything.

163
00:13:26,111 --> 00:13:27,450
Mom.

164
00:13:30,050 --> 00:13:32,591
Mom, why would you say that?

165
00:13:32,591 --> 00:13:33,728
What did I say?

166
00:13:33,728 --> 00:13:36,256
What? Mom... Mom, you keep...

167
00:13:36,256 --> 00:13:37,517
Quit it.

168
00:13:37,517 --> 00:13:39,627
You speak nicely to your mother.

169
00:13:42,108 --> 00:13:44,733
No, what I'm saying is, I...

170
00:13:44,733 --> 00:13:46,322
I, come on, I'm...

171
00:13:46,322 --> 00:13:48,462
Stop stammering and spit it out.

172
00:13:48,462 --> 00:13:50,194
You're annoying me.

173
00:13:50,194 --> 00:13:51,354
But...

174
00:13:52,769 --> 00:13:58,763
I-I haven't even told my friends
I'll miss summer school yet!

175
00:13:59,547 --> 00:14:01,294
Then do it now!

176
00:14:01,294 --> 00:14:03,078
You have your phone, don't you?

177
00:14:11,737 --> 00:14:15,263
Hey, guys... I'm going to be absent.

178
00:14:17,689 --> 00:14:19,545
What? Why?

179
00:14:19,545 --> 00:14:21,755
Did something happen, Ha Yeon?

180
00:14:22,938 --> 00:14:25,741
My Dad's going to the suburbs for a caddie job.

181
00:14:25,741 --> 00:14:28,619
The whole family's going with him.

182
00:14:29,225 --> 00:14:32,392
Oh, no. We can't watch
the movie tomorrow, then.

183
00:14:34,205 --> 00:14:35,801
Yeah...

184
00:14:35,801 --> 00:14:38,572
Hey, then what about my sundress?

185
00:14:38,572 --> 00:14:42,408
I didn't even buy anything new
because you said you'd let me borrow it!

186
00:14:42,408 --> 00:14:46,258
Mi Hee, would you like to
borrow my pink blouse instead?

187
00:14:46,258 --> 00:14:49,758
Kim Ha Yeon! You should've
told me about this sooner!

188
00:14:55,511 --> 00:14:56,705
Right, Mom?

189
00:14:56,705 --> 00:14:59,503
Can you send me 200,000 won real quick?

190
00:14:59,503 --> 00:15:01,433
I want to buy a new game pack.

191
00:15:01,433 --> 00:15:03,386
Sure thing.

192
00:15:03,386 --> 00:15:05,591
Should I transfer it to your bank now?

193
00:15:05,591 --> 00:15:06,638
Yeah.

194
00:15:10,014 --> 00:15:11,038
What're you looking at?

195
00:15:23,464 --> 00:15:26,883
Screw it, she'd pay for that crap
but won't give me 20,000 won for my workbook?

196
00:15:26,883 --> 00:15:28,676
"Screw it?"

197
00:15:28,676 --> 00:15:30,814
Was that meant for me?

198
00:15:30,814 --> 00:15:31,931
Answer me!

199
00:15:31,931 --> 00:15:33,475
"Screw it?"

200
00:15:35,081 --> 00:15:36,782
I can't take this!

201
00:15:36,782 --> 00:15:39,283
This is so messed up!

202
00:15:39,283 --> 00:15:40,635
Be quiet!

203
00:16:00,700 --> 00:16:03,171
Get your act together, Kim Ha Yeon.

204
00:16:03,959 --> 00:16:06,511
It's rude to yell, you rascal!

205
00:16:07,189 --> 00:16:08,405
I'm turning in first.

206
00:16:08,405 --> 00:16:10,301
Of course, Jung Yeon. You must be exhausted.

207
00:16:10,301 --> 00:16:11,721
Get some sleep.

208
00:16:11,721 --> 00:16:14,183
- Where's my room?
- In there.

209
00:16:21,148 --> 00:16:22,260
Hey!

210
00:16:22,260 --> 00:16:24,001
Where are you off to?

211
00:16:24,001 --> 00:16:27,026
What? He went in. Why shouldn't I?

212
00:16:27,026 --> 00:16:28,867
You and he are different.

213
00:16:28,867 --> 00:16:30,685
Come unpack with me.

214
00:16:50,225 --> 00:16:51,550
Careful!

215
00:16:51,550 --> 00:16:52,934
- Why?
- Hey.

216
00:16:52,934 --> 00:16:54,740
That's your brother's bag.

217
00:16:54,740 --> 00:16:57,647
What if there's something important in there?

218
00:17:05,383 --> 00:17:06,710
You little...

219
00:17:06,710 --> 00:17:08,174
Hey, Kim Ha Yeon!

220
00:17:08,174 --> 00:17:09,834
Where are you going?

221
00:17:24,585 --> 00:17:27,053
It's not like I want to die.

222
00:17:46,357 --> 00:17:47,635
Hey, Kim Ha Yeon.

223
00:17:47,635 --> 00:17:49,391
Explain yourself!

224
00:17:49,391 --> 00:17:51,305
Did you seriously just say that to me?

225
00:17:51,305 --> 00:17:54,532
Look, you promised to lend me
that sundress first,

226
00:17:54,532 --> 00:17:57,923
and then scrambled off
with excuses about your dad.

227
00:17:57,923 --> 00:17:59,710
You're the one who should apologize!

228
00:17:59,710 --> 00:18:01,771
"Screw it?"

229
00:18:01,771 --> 00:18:04,697
Hey. Hey. Hey!

230
00:18:08,670 --> 00:18:15,678
[I'm sorry...]

231
00:18:15,678 --> 00:18:17,306
I'm sorry...

232
00:18:31,189 --> 00:18:33,388
I didn't mean it at you.

233
00:18:34,641 --> 00:18:37,658
So why would you say it to me? Pissing me off.

234
00:18:37,658 --> 00:18:38,809
I'm sorry.

235
00:18:38,809 --> 00:18:42,038
I'll lend you that sundress
once summer vacation is over.

236
00:18:42,038 --> 00:18:43,663
- Sorry.
- I don't need that!

237
00:18:43,663 --> 00:18:46,542
I wanted to wear it to my trip with Yun Jae!

238
00:18:46,542 --> 00:18:49,378
I need to buy something new because of you!
I don't even have money!

239
00:18:49,378 --> 00:18:52,174
I have nothing to wear right now.

240
00:19:11,859 --> 00:19:12,945
Well...

241
00:19:13,681 --> 00:19:16,422
I have 50,000 won. Do you want it?

242
00:19:18,191 --> 00:19:19,533
What? Really?

243
00:19:19,533 --> 00:19:21,578
Are you sure?

244
00:19:22,283 --> 00:19:23,413
It's fine.

245
00:19:24,464 --> 00:19:26,696
Thank you so much!

246
00:19:33,814 --> 00:19:36,050
Kim Ha Yeon, you better
get back home right now!

247
00:19:36,050 --> 00:19:41,014
Jung Yeon's missing sleep because of you!
And your Dad needs to work tomorrow!

248
00:19:51,607 --> 00:19:54,319
What would happen if I did die?

249
00:19:58,614 --> 00:20:01,285
Will everyone regret it once I'm gone?

250
00:20:24,640 --> 00:20:26,393
Are you out of your mind?

251
00:20:31,313 --> 00:20:33,503
I highly doubt it.

252
00:20:59,633 --> 00:21:01,053
What's wrong, Yu Gyeom?

253
00:21:03,012 --> 00:21:05,181
Why, was something there? What?

254
00:21:05,181 --> 00:21:06,350
It's nothing.

255
00:21:08,309 --> 00:21:09,685
Are you hungry?

256
00:21:09,685 --> 00:21:10,750
No.

257
00:21:10,750 --> 00:21:12,730
Want your big sis to
make you something at home?

258
00:21:12,730 --> 00:21:14,608
We do have burnt rice at home.

259
00:21:16,515 --> 00:21:18,723
- No.
- Then maybe we should ask Mom to...

260
00:21:18,723 --> 00:21:19,940
Wait, no.

261
00:21:19,940 --> 00:21:21,841
Grandpa bought some red bean jelly.

262
00:21:21,841 --> 00:21:23,617
- Would you like to--
- Sis.

263
00:21:24,957 --> 00:21:26,590
It's fine, really.

264
00:23:23,779 --> 00:23:30,672
The one who will be competing
in the National Swimming Championship...

265
00:23:34,705 --> 00:23:35,960
is Im Jeong Uk.

266
00:23:35,960 --> 00:23:37,234
Give him a round of applause!

267
00:23:45,013 --> 00:23:48,308
You, Jeong Uk, will stay after class
for practice starting today.

268
00:23:48,308 --> 00:23:49,970
- Okay?
- Yes, sir.

269
00:23:49,970 --> 00:23:51,014
Disperse!

270
00:23:51,014 --> 00:23:54,080
- Great work!
- Thank you, sir!

271
00:23:54,080 --> 00:23:55,582
- Good job.
- Thanks.

272
00:23:55,582 --> 00:23:57,765
- Thank you.
- I knew it.

273
00:24:01,312 --> 00:24:04,752
[Congratulations, pro golfer Cho Ji Hyeon,
winner of the Lifestar Championship]

274
00:24:05,819 --> 00:24:07,722
- Careful, sir.
- I must be getting fat.

275
00:24:07,722 --> 00:24:11,637
- Nice seeing you here.
- Good to see you.

276
00:24:27,966 --> 00:24:29,702
Look at the camera.

277
00:24:29,702 --> 00:24:32,193
One, two, three!

278
00:24:35,651 --> 00:24:37,976
Look, Father. Now that's a good photo!

279
00:24:37,976 --> 00:24:40,314
It looks good.

280
00:24:42,347 --> 00:24:46,259
By the way, Father, where's Yu Gyeom?

281
00:24:46,259 --> 00:24:47,969
Hey, Sam Hee!

282
00:24:47,969 --> 00:24:49,071
Yes, Grandpa?

283
00:24:49,071 --> 00:24:50,723
Go get Yu Gyeom, will you?

284
00:24:50,723 --> 00:24:52,544
Auntie wants to see him.

285
00:24:52,544 --> 00:24:54,099
Yes, Grandpa!

286
00:25:15,993 --> 00:25:17,023
Mom!

287
00:25:17,023 --> 00:25:18,058
What is it?

288
00:25:18,058 --> 00:25:19,841
Grandpa's looking for Yu Gyeom.

289
00:25:19,841 --> 00:25:21,356
Go look for him in his room, then.

290
00:25:21,356 --> 00:25:23,006
He's not there. I just checked.

291
00:25:23,006 --> 00:25:27,356
- Not there?
- But Grandpa wants to see him right now.

292
00:25:27,356 --> 00:25:29,405
What about the beach, then?
Did you check there?

293
00:25:29,405 --> 00:25:31,765
- No.
- Well, then go and check now.

294
00:25:31,765 --> 00:25:34,014
Quickly, before he gets mad.

295
00:25:34,014 --> 00:25:35,865
Hey, Cho Yu Gyeom!

296
00:25:37,485 --> 00:25:38,950
Cho Yu Gyeom!

297
00:25:44,605 --> 00:25:45,918
Hey, Cho Yu Gyeom.

298
00:25:49,156 --> 00:25:50,481
What're you up to?

299
00:25:52,305 --> 00:25:54,499
The town is holding a feast for your aunt.

300
00:25:55,694 --> 00:25:57,308
Come on, get up.

301
00:26:01,123 --> 00:26:02,957
I said, get up.

302
00:26:07,407 --> 00:26:09,248
Your hand won't fall off, you know.

303
00:26:11,374 --> 00:26:14,135
I saw your aunt wearing a pig's head.

304
00:26:14,856 --> 00:26:16,896
- Sung Sae Ryeong.
- Yeah? What?

305
00:26:18,690 --> 00:26:22,164
That's my paternal aunt, not my maternal.

306
00:26:22,164 --> 00:26:26,906
By the way, Yu Gyeom,
can't you just hold my hand for once?

307
00:26:26,906 --> 00:26:31,305
By the way, Sae Ryeong,
can't we just walk like this for once?

308
00:26:50,032 --> 00:26:52,025
Look, Yu Gyeom's here!

309
00:26:52,025 --> 00:26:53,529
- Hello.
- You're here, Yu Gyeom!

310
00:26:53,529 --> 00:26:55,155
- There you are, Yu Gyeom.
- Good, that's good.

311
00:26:55,155 --> 00:26:57,324
- What a handsome boy you are!
- How you've grown!

312
00:26:57,324 --> 00:27:00,118
- Hey, Yu Gyeom!
- There you are!

313
00:27:00,118 --> 00:27:03,672
- So handsome!
- You've grown taller!

314
00:27:03,672 --> 00:27:05,404
You're so handsome!

315
00:27:07,417 --> 00:27:09,894
Everyone, sit down and eat.

316
00:27:09,894 --> 00:27:13,053
And Yu Gyeom, come inside.

317
00:27:19,110 --> 00:27:21,211
Excuse me, Father.

318
00:27:21,211 --> 00:27:22,924
Enter.

319
00:27:28,230 --> 00:27:29,847
Put it here.

320
00:27:31,730 --> 00:27:32,763
Where's Sam Hee?

321
00:27:32,763 --> 00:27:36,305
She's out running an errand right now.

322
00:27:36,305 --> 00:27:39,614
Give her a ride. It's hot out.

323
00:27:44,860 --> 00:27:47,074
Sit up straight.

324
00:27:50,335 --> 00:27:54,914
Your tutor came by this morning.

325
00:27:54,914 --> 00:27:57,925
I heard you're good at that thing you do.

326
00:27:58,844 --> 00:27:59,883
Swimming, sir.

327
00:27:59,883 --> 00:28:00,980
Yes, that.

328
00:28:00,980 --> 00:28:06,815
He asked me to let you enter the competition.

329
00:28:07,546 --> 00:28:09,048
Are you going to?

330
00:28:11,252 --> 00:28:12,942
No, sir. No.

331
00:28:14,022 --> 00:28:16,156
Are you sure you don't want to?

332
00:28:16,156 --> 00:28:18,230
Yes, I'm sure.

333
00:28:18,230 --> 00:28:19,369
Good.

334
00:28:19,369 --> 00:28:22,097
You just can't, Yu Gyeom.

335
00:28:23,324 --> 00:28:26,910
As for why, you must know, right?

336
00:28:26,910 --> 00:28:29,450
Because I'm a part of this family.

337
00:28:29,450 --> 00:28:30,752
Correct.

338
00:28:30,752 --> 00:28:34,433
You have to stay dedicated to this house.

339
00:28:34,433 --> 00:28:36,090
Right?

340
00:28:36,090 --> 00:28:38,116
Right, although my aunt doesn't need to.

341
00:28:38,116 --> 00:28:40,798
She wasn't born into this family!

342
00:28:40,798 --> 00:28:42,584
And I was. I know.

343
00:28:44,910 --> 00:28:46,850
That's enough.

344
00:28:46,850 --> 00:28:48,289
You may leave.

345
00:29:00,924 --> 00:29:02,296
Yu Gyeom!

346
00:29:03,443 --> 00:29:05,730
Yu Gyeom, how have you been?

347
00:29:05,730 --> 00:29:08,571
Have you been well? Yeah?

348
00:29:08,571 --> 00:29:11,173
Be polite, Yu Gyeom. Answer me.

349
00:29:11,173 --> 00:29:12,950
Yes, I've been...

350
00:29:14,850 --> 00:29:15,943
well.

351
00:29:15,943 --> 00:29:17,924
My dearest boy!

352
00:29:17,924 --> 00:29:20,864
Come on, keep your eyes on me.

353
00:29:20,864 --> 00:29:23,530
My goodness, how long has it been?

354
00:29:23,530 --> 00:29:26,473
Your auntie missed you so much!

355
00:29:26,473 --> 00:29:28,981
We met last month
for the ancestral memorial rite.

356
00:29:28,981 --> 00:29:30,842
So it's been about three weeks.

357
00:29:30,842 --> 00:29:31,873
Truly?

358
00:29:31,873 --> 00:29:33,772
Three weeks?

359
00:29:33,772 --> 00:29:39,674
Yu Gyeom, your auntie starts missing you
so badly after only a week apart!

360
00:29:39,674 --> 00:29:42,545
My dear boy.

361
00:29:42,545 --> 00:29:44,141
Yu Gyeom, you know, right?

362
00:29:44,141 --> 00:29:45,577
You're my boy.

363
00:29:45,577 --> 00:29:47,718
My son, that I bore through my heart.

364
00:29:47,718 --> 00:29:49,602
You know that, right?

365
00:29:55,700 --> 00:29:57,339
You!

366
00:29:57,339 --> 00:29:59,165
You there!

367
00:29:59,165 --> 00:30:01,110
Why aren't you bowing to me?

368
00:30:02,524 --> 00:30:04,527
Yes, ma'am.

369
00:30:04,527 --> 00:30:06,353
Greetings.

370
00:30:08,676 --> 00:30:09,749
Oh, dear!

371
00:30:10,635 --> 00:30:12,891
I never knew you could laugh, my boy!

372
00:30:15,092 --> 00:30:17,099
Goodness me, he just laughed!

373
00:30:19,192 --> 00:30:20,908
What a pretty laugh you have!

374
00:30:34,729 --> 00:30:37,711
Mi Hee and Yun Ah's girls' day out!

375
00:30:37,711 --> 00:30:40,680
So bummed out that Ha Yeon wasn't there.

376
00:30:40,680 --> 00:30:42,997
How's it going in that backwater town, Ha Yeon?

377
00:30:42,997 --> 00:30:44,456
Having fun?

378
00:30:46,417 --> 00:30:49,100
No, it's really boring.

379
00:30:52,641 --> 00:30:54,917
But honestly, it's no different
from being with you guys.

380
00:30:58,393 --> 00:31:00,162
Hey, Kim Ha Yeon!

381
00:31:06,855 --> 00:31:09,629
Darling, what time is the tee off tomorrow?

382
00:31:10,343 --> 00:31:11,648
6 o'clock.

383
00:31:11,648 --> 00:31:13,251
What do you want?

384
00:31:13,251 --> 00:31:15,956
See that rice cake over there? Portion it out.

385
00:31:15,956 --> 00:31:18,167
Pack them up nicely.

386
00:31:18,167 --> 00:31:21,077
Make sure you stack them, two in a bag.

387
00:31:22,251 --> 00:31:25,682
Can't you make him do stuff like this?

388
00:31:25,682 --> 00:31:26,747
What?

389
00:31:27,755 --> 00:31:30,539
I need to study, too.

390
00:31:30,539 --> 00:31:33,930
I need to make up for the classes I'm missing,
or my grades will suffer.

391
00:31:33,930 --> 00:31:37,069
You can study after you pack the rice cake.

392
00:31:38,723 --> 00:31:40,896
This is so frustrating.

393
00:31:44,783 --> 00:31:46,118
What now?

394
00:32:16,101 --> 00:32:18,680
It's already past midnight.

395
00:32:18,680 --> 00:32:21,360
When will I get to sleep
if I have to study after all this?

396
00:32:21,360 --> 00:32:24,216
Just tell Jung Yeon to do it.
He's playing games right now!

397
00:32:24,216 --> 00:32:28,531
His hands are too big
for delicate chores like that.

398
00:32:29,205 --> 00:32:30,625
What?

399
00:32:30,625 --> 00:32:32,735
Stop slacking off, come on!

400
00:32:34,718 --> 00:32:38,090
I wonder how he plays mobile games
with such huge hands.

401
00:32:39,549 --> 00:32:41,243
Don't you talk back to me like that!

402
00:32:41,243 --> 00:32:42,736
I should punish you!

403
00:32:42,736 --> 00:32:45,239
Why would you hit me?

404
00:32:47,211 --> 00:32:50,174
I don't need such a crappy mom.

405
00:32:50,174 --> 00:32:52,921
I don't need these crappy friends.

406
00:32:52,921 --> 00:32:54,908
I'd rather be an orphan and an outcast.

407
00:32:54,908 --> 00:32:58,098
I'll make it out of here. I'll escape,

408
00:32:58,790 --> 00:33:01,424
and I will change my fate.

409
00:33:01,424 --> 00:33:03,477
Whatever it takes...

410
00:33:24,252 --> 00:33:25,399
But...

411
00:33:26,713 --> 00:33:29,665
How does one go about changing their fate?

412
00:33:42,062 --> 00:33:44,536
- Mom.
- Yes?

413
00:33:44,536 --> 00:33:48,993
Why do we call her "aunt?"

414
00:33:51,711 --> 00:33:54,057
She's not really my aunt,
so what's up with that?

415
00:33:54,057 --> 00:33:56,576
She's just Father's first love.

416
00:33:56,576 --> 00:33:57,800
Yu Gyeom.

417
00:33:57,800 --> 00:33:59,754
And isn't she just horrible?

418
00:33:59,754 --> 00:34:03,060
She acts like she runs the place,
even though she's not really in power.

419
00:34:03,060 --> 00:34:04,297
She's so rude to you, too.

420
00:34:04,297 --> 00:34:07,202
Calling you "hey" and "you there."

421
00:34:09,214 --> 00:34:13,118
Actually, I do think she's horrible, too.

422
00:34:13,118 --> 00:34:15,254
I hate her guts.

423
00:34:17,150 --> 00:34:20,023
Why don't you leave the family?

424
00:34:21,080 --> 00:34:22,585
What a shame.

425
00:34:23,468 --> 00:34:26,547
I already left my family for this one.

426
00:34:26,547 --> 00:34:29,374
I heard that gray divorces
are all the rage these days.

427
00:34:31,024 --> 00:34:33,346
You're funny.

428
00:34:37,697 --> 00:34:39,658
- And, Mom?
- Yeah?

429
00:34:40,787 --> 00:34:47,588
In celebration of your divorce,
can I get a phone?

430
00:34:49,780 --> 00:34:51,927
- What?
- Come on.

431
00:34:51,927 --> 00:34:54,490
I'm 18 years old
without a phone in this day and age.

432
00:34:54,490 --> 00:34:58,612
It's wild that I have to write on paper
and use a carrier pigeon to contact people.

433
00:35:01,226 --> 00:35:02,851
Silly boy.

434
00:35:03,618 --> 00:35:06,849
Is this what you were getting at all this time?

435
00:35:06,849 --> 00:35:08,176
Was it so obvious?

436
00:35:08,176 --> 00:35:10,527
You've become so sly.

437
00:35:10,527 --> 00:35:11,858
Ask your Grandpa.

438
00:35:11,858 --> 00:35:13,194
I do have a secret of birth.

439
00:35:13,194 --> 00:35:15,062
No way.

440
00:35:19,058 --> 00:35:20,806
And a special talent.

441
00:36:20,261 --> 00:36:22,330
Cho Yu Gyeom!

442
00:36:23,417 --> 00:36:26,997
Cho Yu Gyeom!

443
00:36:26,997 --> 00:36:28,301
Get out here right now!

444
00:36:28,301 --> 00:36:30,980
Come back out, young master!

445
00:36:30,980 --> 00:36:32,834
What's gotten into you?

446
00:36:32,834 --> 00:36:36,887
I have a beautiful girlfriend,
and fitting friends, but...

447
00:36:36,887 --> 00:36:40,187
What are you doing in there?

448
00:36:42,409 --> 00:36:44,342
It's all so boring.

449
00:36:51,641 --> 00:36:52,794
No.

450
00:36:52,794 --> 00:36:55,935
I already told you this is a hard no.

451
00:36:55,935 --> 00:36:57,728
Whatever, don't do it, then.

452
00:36:57,728 --> 00:36:59,146
Are you leaving?

453
00:36:59,859 --> 00:37:00,893
Yeah.

454
00:37:00,893 --> 00:37:02,554
Don't be like that.

455
00:37:02,554 --> 00:37:04,926
Stay here with me for a while.

456
00:37:04,926 --> 00:37:06,184
What's there to do?

457
00:37:06,184 --> 00:37:08,667
Talk. About you and me.

458
00:37:08,667 --> 00:37:09,860
What do you say?

459
00:37:10,620 --> 00:37:13,518
We know everything about each other's lives.
What's there to talk about?

460
00:37:14,507 --> 00:37:15,900
Cho Yu Gyeom.

461
00:37:18,499 --> 00:37:20,333
Why? What?

462
00:37:21,755 --> 00:37:25,886
Then what are you dating me for?

463
00:37:57,692 --> 00:37:59,601
Mom! Everyone's here!

464
00:37:59,601 --> 00:38:01,450
Should I bring this out now?

465
00:38:01,450 --> 00:38:02,847
Where's Yu Gyeom?

466
00:38:03,613 --> 00:38:06,844
Well, he's not there.

467
00:38:06,844 --> 00:38:08,150
What?

468
00:38:17,045 --> 00:38:18,884
Mom.

469
00:38:37,857 --> 00:38:39,882
You can have the rice cake on the table.

470
00:38:39,882 --> 00:38:42,785
I'm going into town
to get some clothes for your brother.

471
00:38:42,785 --> 00:38:46,221
Also, don't forget to make him breakfast
when he wakes up!

472
00:39:06,803 --> 00:39:08,518
Where's Yu Gyeom?

473
00:39:09,258 --> 00:39:10,942
He's... well...

474
00:39:10,942 --> 00:39:12,920
He's just...

475
00:39:12,920 --> 00:39:15,508
- Father.
- You should eat, Father.

476
00:39:16,408 --> 00:39:18,439
Why isn't Yu Gyeom here?

477
00:39:18,439 --> 00:39:21,949
I sent him out to run an errand, that's all.

478
00:39:21,949 --> 00:39:23,585
He'll be here soon.

479
00:39:23,585 --> 00:39:25,225
Go ahead and eat, Father.

480
00:39:27,765 --> 00:39:29,150
What's wrong?

481
00:39:31,786 --> 00:39:34,035
Alright. Let's eat.

482
00:39:38,960 --> 00:39:41,209
Your brother this, your brother that,
all day and night!

483
00:39:41,209 --> 00:39:44,170
I'd rather she was my stepmom.
That way I'd go look for my real one.

484
00:39:44,170 --> 00:39:46,075
I can't believe this is the mom I'm stuck with!

485
00:39:46,075 --> 00:39:48,952
This is just the worst!

486
00:41:03,336 --> 00:41:04,384
By the way, Ha Yeon.

487
00:41:04,384 --> 00:41:07,087
50,000 won isn't enough to buy anything at all!

488
00:41:07,087 --> 00:41:09,002
Have you got any more?

489
00:41:09,002 --> 00:41:12,878
I spent all my money
buying new sneakers for Yun Jae.

490
00:41:12,878 --> 00:41:16,331
I'm not asking you to give me money.
I just want to borrow it!

491
00:41:17,394 --> 00:41:20,350
Sure, you broke tramp.

492
00:41:25,566 --> 00:41:27,989
Change my fate? What a joke.

493
00:41:34,867 --> 00:41:35,997
Sure.

494
00:41:45,086 --> 00:41:46,271
What's that?

495
00:41:48,208 --> 00:41:49,453
Is that a person?

496
00:41:54,698 --> 00:41:56,006
Hey, there!

497
00:41:57,721 --> 00:41:58,997
Someone...

498
00:42:23,958 --> 00:42:25,352
Wait!

499
00:42:27,881 --> 00:42:29,073
Hey.

500
00:42:30,047 --> 00:42:31,519
Hey, you!

501
00:42:36,299 --> 00:42:38,219
Are you okay?

502
00:42:39,478 --> 00:42:41,176
Are you alive?

503
00:42:45,605 --> 00:42:47,237
Oh, you're alive!

504
00:42:47,237 --> 00:42:49,145
Thank goodness!

505
00:43:00,536 --> 00:43:03,542
I thought you were drowning, and...

506
00:43:03,542 --> 00:43:04,813
Listen.

507
00:43:06,124 --> 00:43:09,955
If you ever see someone drowning,
you don't just jump in.

508
00:43:10,689 --> 00:43:12,594
You call emergency services.

509
00:43:17,488 --> 00:43:20,285
By the way,
why are you talking to me so informally?

510
00:43:22,558 --> 00:43:24,599
Mister?

511
00:43:28,356 --> 00:43:30,347
You don't know me.

512
00:43:34,654 --> 00:43:35,946
Do you?

513
00:43:37,317 --> 00:43:38,724
Are you a senior?

514
00:43:39,842 --> 00:43:40,899
No.

515
00:43:41,826 --> 00:43:43,261
So I'm not in the wrong.

516
00:44:17,989 --> 00:44:19,532
Do you know Upo Country Club?

517
00:44:19,532 --> 00:44:21,993
It's a golf course.

518
00:44:21,993 --> 00:44:23,718
Is that where you came from?

519
00:44:23,718 --> 00:44:24,936
Yeah.

520
00:44:24,936 --> 00:44:27,127
I don't know my way back.

521
00:44:27,993 --> 00:44:32,406
You came all the way here from there,
but don't know how to get there from here?

522
00:44:34,460 --> 00:44:37,015
I used the map on my phone.

523
00:44:38,919 --> 00:44:40,895
But I soaked it in seawater.

524
00:44:43,681 --> 00:44:45,660
Do you know how to get there?

525
00:44:46,707 --> 00:44:50,920
Just keep walking that way
and cross at the 16-lane road.

526
00:44:52,888 --> 00:44:54,030
Thanks.

527
00:45:02,658 --> 00:45:04,105
I'm freezing.

528
00:45:13,252 --> 00:45:14,256
Hey.

529
00:45:22,345 --> 00:45:23,481
Here.

530
00:45:27,725 --> 00:45:29,497
Put it on, and follow me.

531
00:45:50,289 --> 00:45:51,958
We're here.

532
00:45:53,042 --> 00:45:54,111
Thanks.

533
00:45:56,295 --> 00:45:57,883
No need. You can take it with you.

534
00:45:58,631 --> 00:46:00,466
But it's yours.

535
00:46:00,466 --> 00:46:01,970
It's fine.

536
00:46:35,209 --> 00:46:36,764
Hey.

537
00:46:36,764 --> 00:46:38,023
Yeah?

538
00:46:38,023 --> 00:46:40,326
Do you want to give it back to me?

539
00:46:41,153 --> 00:46:42,181
What?

540
00:46:42,181 --> 00:46:43,968
My shirt.

541
00:46:43,968 --> 00:46:45,625
Do you want to return it?

542
00:46:46,338 --> 00:46:48,863
Well, yeah, it's yours.

543
00:46:54,895 --> 00:46:56,925
How long are you staying here?

544
00:46:59,817 --> 00:47:02,406
Until the end of summer vacation, probably.

545
00:47:03,362 --> 00:47:05,031
That's...

546
00:47:05,031 --> 00:47:06,705
three weeks from now, right?

547
00:47:06,705 --> 00:47:08,117
Yeah.

548
00:47:08,117 --> 00:47:10,270
I'll be around here every evening.

549
00:47:11,412 --> 00:47:12,637
What?

550
00:47:12,637 --> 00:47:16,646
Nothing, just letting you know
I'll be around after 9 o'clock.

551
00:47:16,646 --> 00:47:18,104
Someplace nearby.

552
00:47:18,104 --> 00:47:22,909
Like the beach, or the alleyways
behind the beach.

553
00:47:22,909 --> 00:47:24,350
Just around.

554
00:47:25,104 --> 00:47:27,472
- So what do you mean by--
- What I'm saying is,

555
00:47:27,472 --> 00:47:31,195
if we cross paths again on any evening,
you can give it back then.

556
00:47:33,270 --> 00:47:37,937
But this is a huge neighborhood.
The chances are pretty slim.

557
00:47:37,937 --> 00:47:39,577
We'll see each other when we do.

558
00:47:44,111 --> 00:47:45,362
Hey!

559
00:47:57,041 --> 00:47:59,120
I'll be around here every evening.

560
00:48:01,080 --> 00:48:05,016
Nothing, just letting you know
I'll be around after 9 o'clock.

561
00:48:19,656 --> 00:48:21,996
[Biographies of Royal Consorts]

562
00:48:22,862 --> 00:48:25,622
[Taejo Wang Geon]
[The Heart Sutra]

563
00:48:51,595 --> 00:48:53,206
Are you okay?

564
00:48:55,128 --> 00:48:56,577
You came here from Seoul?

565
00:48:57,280 --> 00:48:58,517
Why?

566
00:49:00,285 --> 00:49:02,018
Because it's summer vacation.

567
00:49:14,910 --> 00:49:17,985
Darling, what time is the tee off tomorrow?

568
00:49:19,806 --> 00:49:21,853
5:30 in the morning.

569
00:49:22,930 --> 00:49:25,647
- Well, then I'll...
- Mom.

570
00:49:25,647 --> 00:49:27,358
What's the address for this place?

571
00:49:27,358 --> 00:49:29,250
I need to receive a package.

572
00:49:30,320 --> 00:49:31,971
The address...

573
00:49:32,911 --> 00:49:34,927
Gyeongsangbuk-do?

574
00:49:34,927 --> 00:49:36,852
Ha Yeon!

575
00:49:36,852 --> 00:49:39,175
Search up the address, will you?

576
00:49:40,513 --> 00:49:42,216
Ha Yeon!

577
00:49:53,132 --> 00:49:55,492
[How does one go about changing their fate?]

578
00:50:06,128 --> 00:50:07,337
Kim Ha Yeon!

579
00:50:09,476 --> 00:50:12,727
What are you doing?
I told you to look up the address!

580
00:50:12,727 --> 00:50:14,311
Where are you off to?

581
00:50:14,311 --> 00:50:16,403
Do you even know what time it is?

582
00:50:16,403 --> 00:50:18,320
9 o'clock!

583
00:50:21,944 --> 00:50:24,095
That little rascal!

584
00:50:30,778 --> 00:50:32,358
Yu Gyeom, Grandpa wants...

585
00:50:32,358 --> 00:50:33,410
No.

586
00:50:33,410 --> 00:50:35,128
What do you mean, "no"?

587
00:50:35,128 --> 00:50:36,742
I said, Grandpa wants...

588
00:50:36,742 --> 00:50:37,817
Quiet.

589
00:50:37,817 --> 00:50:39,787
Where are you going? Yu Gyeom!

590
00:50:39,787 --> 00:50:41,374
Cho Yu Gyeom!

591
00:50:49,463 --> 00:50:51,369
I like movies.

592
00:51:00,849 --> 00:51:02,625
I believe in fate.

593
00:51:05,479 --> 00:51:09,517
I await a prince on a white horse
or my rich birth parents to come find me.

594
00:51:09,517 --> 00:51:14,091
I believe that one day,
a miracle may happen to me.

595
00:51:14,945 --> 00:51:16,414
I believe.

596
00:51:18,089 --> 00:51:20,635
I believe in fate, and this summer.

597
00:51:20,635 --> 00:51:23,451
In everything that's going
to happen this summer.

598
00:51:24,581 --> 00:51:28,209
In all the magical moments
that are to come this summer.

599
00:51:29,378 --> 00:51:31,133
- I wish for them.
- I wish for them.

600
00:51:52,067 --> 00:51:54,487
Letting you know
I'll be around after 9 o'clock.

601
00:51:54,487 --> 00:51:55,934
Someplace nearby.

602
00:51:55,934 --> 00:52:00,710
Like the beach, or the alleyways
behind the beach.

603
00:52:00,710 --> 00:52:02,261
Just around.

604
00:52:15,758 --> 00:52:17,288
What're you gawking at?

605
00:52:20,971 --> 00:52:22,662
Hey, are you a student?

606
00:52:22,662 --> 00:52:23,932
Where are you going?

607
00:52:23,932 --> 00:52:28,349
- You're cute.
- Come over here, let's play. Want a drink?

608
00:52:28,349 --> 00:52:29,688
Hey, I asked where you're going!

609
00:52:29,688 --> 00:52:31,412
- It's late.
- Come here.

610
00:52:31,412 --> 00:52:32,652
- Hey, cutie!
- Go home!

611
00:52:32,652 --> 00:52:34,755
- Are you deaf?
- Pretty girl!

612
00:52:34,755 --> 00:52:36,605
It's dangerous out here. I'll take you home.

613
00:52:36,605 --> 00:52:39,050
- Get over here, let's have fun.
- Look here, I love you!

614
00:52:39,050 --> 00:52:41,161
- I'll take you home!
- Cut it out!

615
00:52:41,161 --> 00:52:42,829
- Come on!
- You're scaring her.

616
00:52:42,829 --> 00:52:44,602
Come home with me.

617
00:52:44,602 --> 00:52:47,385
- Stop saying that, bro.
- I'm just messing with her.

618
00:53:15,573 --> 00:53:17,275
What about my shirt?

619
00:53:28,122 --> 00:53:29,244
It's this way!

620
00:53:29,244 --> 00:53:30,413
No, not there.

621
00:53:30,413 --> 00:53:31,707
This way!

622
00:53:31,707 --> 00:53:33,783
What the hell, she's not here!

623
00:53:33,783 --> 00:53:35,989
No, I said it's this way.

624
00:53:35,989 --> 00:53:37,839
I saw her go this way.

625
00:53:43,303 --> 00:53:44,460
She's not here.

626
00:53:44,460 --> 00:53:47,103
Look, I have 20/20 vision.

627
00:53:47,103 --> 00:53:48,823
- That adds up to 40.
- What do we do?

628
00:53:48,823 --> 00:53:53,631
I saw the girl go this way,
and a boy followed her inside.

629
00:53:56,150 --> 00:53:57,985
I swear I saw it!

630
00:53:57,985 --> 00:54:00,345
Why are you guys ganging up on me?

631
00:54:00,345 --> 00:54:02,772
Then they must be hiding.

632
00:54:13,417 --> 00:54:15,239
Did you guys know about that door?

633
00:54:15,239 --> 00:54:18,017
What? A door? Where?

634
00:54:19,715 --> 00:54:21,136
Let's check it out.

635
00:54:26,430 --> 00:54:27,838
See? I told you!

636
00:54:27,838 --> 00:54:30,058
They definitely went this way!

637
00:54:30,058 --> 00:54:32,236
Look again!

638
00:54:32,236 --> 00:54:33,601
There's nobody here.

639
00:54:33,601 --> 00:54:34,922
You!

640
00:54:34,922 --> 00:54:37,444
Are you sure you saw them go this way?

641
00:54:37,444 --> 00:54:39,976
I did, I'm sure!

642
00:54:39,976 --> 00:54:41,458
I...

643
00:54:41,458 --> 00:54:43,907
- I swear I saw them.
- He's lying.

644
00:54:43,907 --> 00:54:45,301
Just a load of crap.

645
00:54:45,301 --> 00:54:46,924
Are there any other doors here?

646
00:54:46,924 --> 00:54:48,859
Fat chance.

647
00:54:49,759 --> 00:54:51,776
I swear I saw them!

648
00:55:00,088 --> 00:55:02,857
Whatever, man. Let's get back to drinking.

649
00:55:04,230 --> 00:55:05,596
Aren't you coming?

650
00:55:05,596 --> 00:55:07,186
But I swear...

651
00:56:06,905 --> 00:56:08,874
I think they're gone now.

652
00:56:20,460 --> 00:56:22,511
I believe in fate.

653
00:56:24,208 --> 00:56:25,369
Sorry.

654
00:56:26,971 --> 00:56:28,150
What for?

655
00:56:32,180 --> 00:56:34,575
I forgot to bring your shirt.

656
00:56:37,811 --> 00:56:39,060
I'm sorry.

657
00:56:40,658 --> 00:56:42,279
I don't care.

658
00:56:47,466 --> 00:56:49,170
I don't care anymore.

659
00:56:56,121 --> 00:57:00,299
I... But I've never done this before.

660
00:57:01,489 --> 00:57:03,010
Do you want to stop?

661
00:57:12,888 --> 00:57:15,783
In everything that's going
to happen this summer.

662
00:57:32,269 --> 00:57:35,582
In all the magical moments
that are to come this summer.

663
00:57:40,666 --> 00:57:42,216
I wish for them.

664
00:57:43,210 --> 00:57:44,765
I wish for them.
